<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francesco Maria Pico</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1688">1688</a>–<a href="/years/1747">1747</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francesco Maria Pico (1688–1747) was the last Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirandola">Mirandola</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a> he sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and in 1708 Emperor Joseph I deprived him of the duchy. In 1710 Mirandola was sold to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rinaldo-d-este-duke-of-modena">Rinaldo d'Este, Duke of Modena</a>, and Francesco Maria spent the rest of his life in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francesco-maria-pico.jpg" alt="Francesco Maria Pico" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francesco_Maria_II_Pico.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
